1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,640
Man: Excuse me. Would you mind if I asked you some questions

2
00:00:06,500 --> 00:00:08,520
We're doing a survey on transport.

3
00:00:08,520 --> 00:00:10,720
Sadie: Yes, that's OK.

4
00:00:10,720 --> 00:00:13,460
Man: First of all, can I take your name?

5
00:00:13,460 --> 00:00:16,500
Sadie: Yes. It's Sadie Jones.

6
00:00:16,500 --> 00:00:20,329
Man: Thanks very much. And could I have your date of birth -

7
00:00:20,329 --> 00:00:23,520
just the year will do, actually. Is that all right?

8
00:00:23,520 --> 00:00:28,600
Sadie: Yes, that's fine. It's 1991.

9
00:00:28,600 --> 00:00:32,130
Man: So next your postcode, please.

10
00:00:32,130 --> 00:00:38,200
Sadie: It's DW30 7YZ.

11
00:00:38,200 --> 00:00:41,960
Man: Great. Thanks. Is that in Wells?

12
00:00:41,960 --> 00:00:47,280
Sadie: No it's actually in Harborne - Wells isn't far from there, though.

13
00:00:47,280 --> 00:00:52,100
Man: I really like that area. My grandmother lived there when I was a kid.

14
00:00:52,100 --> 00:00:54,390
Sadie: Yes, it is nice.

15
00:00:54,390 --> 00:01:01,213
Man: Right, so now I want to ask you some questions about how you travelled here today.

16
00:01:01,213 --> 00:01:03,220
Did you use public transport?

17
00:01:03,220 --> 00:01:05,660
Sadie: Yes. I came by bus.

18
00:01:05,660 --> 00:01:11,610
Man: OK. And that was today. It's the 24th of April, isn't it?

19
00:01:11,610 --> 00:01:18,420
Sadie: Isn't it the 25th? No, actually, you're right.

20
00:01:18,420 --> 00:01:21,440
Man: And what was the reason for your trip today

21
00:01:21,900 --> 00:01:24,130
I can see you've got some shopping with you.

22
00:01:24,130 --> 00:01:26,480
Sadie: Yes. I did some shopping

23
00:01:26,980 --> 00:01:31,680
but the main reason I came here was to go to the dentist.

24
00:01:31,680 --> 00:01:35,250
Man: That's not much fun. Hope it was nothing serious.

25
00:01:35,250 --> 00:01:38,610
Sadie: No, it was just a check-up. It's fine.

26
00:01:38,610 --> 00:01:43,050
Man: Good. Do you normally travel by bus into the city centre?

27
00:01:43,050 --> 00:01:49,920
Sadie: Yes. I stopped driving in ages ago because parking was so difficult to find

28
00:01:50,300 --> 00:01:52,260
and it costs so much.

29
00:01:52,260 --> 00:01:53,380
Man: I see.

30
00:01:53,380 --> 00:01:58,860
Sadie: The bus is much more convenient too. It only takes about 30 minutes.

31
00:01:58,860 --> 00:02:02,620
Man: That's good. So where did you start your journey?

32
00:02:02,620 --> 00:02:06,380
Sadie: At the bus stop on Claxby Street.

33
00:02:06,380 --> 00:02:10,790
Man: Is that C-L-A-X-B-Y?

34
00:02:10,790 --> 00:02:15,000
Sadie: That's right.

35
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:19,610
Man: And how satisfied with the service are you? Do you have any complaints?

36
00:02:19,610 --> 00:02:25,760
Sadie: Well, as I said, it's very convenient and quick when it's on time

37
00:02:26,160 --> 00:02:28,897
but this morning it was late.

38
00:02:28,897 --> 00:02:31,430
Only about 10 minutes, but still.

39
00:02:31,430 --> 00:02:35,760
Man: Yes, I understand that's annoying. And what about the timetable

40
00:02:36,100 --> 00:02:38,100
Do you have any comments about that?

41
00:02:38,100 --> 00:02:43,420
Sadie: Mmm. I suppose I mainly use the bus during the day

42
00:02:43,980 --> 00:02:47,046
but any time I've been in town in the evening -

43
00:02:47,046 --> 00:02:54,200
for dinner or at the cinema - I've noticed you have to wait a long time for a bus

44
00:02:54,640 --> 00:02:56,380
there aren't that many.

45
00:02:56,380 --> 00:03:02,120
Man: OK, thanks. So now I'd like to ask you about your car use.

46
00:03:02,120 --> 00:03:07,480
Sadie: Well, I have got a car but I don't use it that often.

47
00:03:07,480 --> 00:03:09,981
Mainly just to go to the supermarket.

48
00:03:09,981 --> 00:03:12,125
But that's about it really.

49
00:03:12,125 --> 00:03:16,770
My husband uses it at the weekends to go to the golf club.

50
00:03:16,770 --> 00:03:18,570
Man: And what about a bicycle?

51
00:03:18,570 --> 00:03:21,230
Sadie: I don't actually have one at the moment.

52
00:03:21,230 --> 00:03:25,270
Man: What about the city bikes you can rent? Do you ever use those?

53
00:03:25,270 --> 00:03:29,805
Sadie: No - I'm not keen on cycling there because of all the pollution.

54
00:03:29,805 --> 00:03:35,960
But I would like to get a bike - it would be good to use it to get to work.

55
00:03:35,960 --> 00:03:38,410
Man: So why haven't you got one now?

56
00:03:38,410 --> 00:03:40,903
Sadie: Well, I live in a flat -

57
00:03:40,903 --> 00:03:44,920
on the second floor and it doesn't have any storage

58
00:03:45,380 --> 00:03:49,450
so we'd have to leave it in the hall outside the flat.

59
00:03:49,450 --> 00:03:53,050
Man: I see. OK. Well, I think that's all...
